indowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" nowrap=\"nowrap\" width=\"8%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">17q11.2</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 8.14%; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" nowrap=\"nowrap\" width=\"8%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><em>NF1</em></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 8.12%; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" nowrap=\"nowrap\" width=\"8%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">613113</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.14%; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" nowrap=\"nowrap\" width=\"9%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Neurofibromin (NF1)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.22%; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" nowrap=\"nowrap\" width=\"14%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Negative regulator of RAS/MAPK pathway</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 15.22%; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"15%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Malignant peripheral nerve sheath tumour, high-grade glioma, juvenile myelomonocytic leukaemia, rhabdomyosarcoma, glomus tumours of the digits, gastrointestinal stromal tumours, phaeochromocytoma, breast cancer in females, duodenal neuroendocrine tumours</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 9.62%; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; mso-border-bottom-alt: solid windowtext .5pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" valign=\"top\" width=\"9%\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Low-grade glioma (including optic pathway glioma), neurofibroma (including plexiform neurofibroma and atypical neurofibroma&nbsp;/ atypical neurofibromatous neoplasms of uncertain biological potential)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">AD, autosomal dominant; AR, autosomal recessive; n/a, not applicable.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><sup>a</sup>Not a cancer predisposition syndrome (i.e. not listed in OMIM as a specific separate syndrome) but is associated with increased risk owing to pathogenic variants in this gene.</p>",
